                    out_point:              `A single point estimate from the one method you trust most`,
                    out_anchor:             `Whatever lands inside the €22–28 banker range — back-solve to fit`,
                    key_fade:               `Revenue-growth durability (the fade) — the biggest swing factor and the one the moat defends`,
                    key_wacc:               `WACC — a defensible secondary driver`,
                    key_none:               `None — the base case is solid enough to stand alone`,

                    r4_news_label:          `A rival AI energy platform just launched and your largest customer (8% of revenue) is reviewing its contract. What do you do to the valuation?`,
                    r4_indep_label:         `Aurial's advisory head hints a “constructive” note would help the banking relationship. Your model says hold. What do you publish?`,
                    r4_rating_label:        `Settle the call: rating, price target and a 12-month horizon`,
                    r4_defence_label:       `IC defence: how firmly do you defend the valuation, the key assumption and the rating against challenge? (%)`,
                    news_retest:            `Re-test the growth-durability assumption and concentration risk — adjust the fade and the range, then re-publish`,
                    news_hold:              `Publish the same number — the news is noise and the model already covers it`,
                    news_panic:             `Slash the valuation to the DCF floor — the moat is clearly gone`,
                    indep_independent:      `Publish what the model supports and document the independence — credibility is the franchise's core asset`,
                    indep_soften:           `Soften to “buy” at €28 — the relationship matters and one note won't hurt`,
                    indep_withdraw:         `Withdraw coverage to avoid the conflict entirely`,
                    rating_hold:            `Hold — central estimate near the lower-mid of the range, fairly priced for the risk`,
